<a id=3D"geospatial-other-charts" data-hs-anchor=3D"true"></a>
<h2>6. Geospatial &amp; other charts</h2>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<a id=3D"geographic-heatmap" data-hs-anchor=3D"true"></a><hr>
<h3><br>Geographic heatmap</h3>
<p>Alternative names: <em>hot spot map</em>, <em>geo heat map</em>, <em>den=
sity heatmap</em></p>
<h4 style=3D"font-size: 21px;"><strong><em><span style=3D"color: #434343;">=
<br><img src=3D"https://www.datylon.com/hs-fs/hubfs/Datylon%20Website2020/B=
logs/80%20types%20of%20charts%20and%20graphs/charts%20iso%20links/80%20type=
s%20of%20charts%20examples%20%E2%80%93%20Geographic%20heatmap.png?width=3D6=
00&amp;height=3D600&amp;name=3D80%20types%20of%20charts%20examples%20%E2%80=
%93%20Geographic%20heatmap.png" width=3D"600" height=3D"600" loading=3D"laz=
y" alt=3D"80 types of charts examples =E2=80=93 Geographic heatmap" style=
=3D"height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-=
right: auto; display: block;"><br><br>What is a geographic heatmap?</span><=
/em></strong></h4>
<p>A geographic heatmap is a geographical representation of data that demon=
strates where something occurs, specifying the areas of data=E2=80=99s high=
 and low density. Geo heatmap does not limit displaying geospatial data to =
specified boundaries. Therefore, using the data=E2=80=99s location radius, =
it can cover a small and specific geographic area, as well as large regions=
, such as oceans or coasts. It uses color to highlight the areas of occurre=
nce.</p>
<h4><strong><em><span>When should you use a geographic heatmap?</span></em>=
</strong></h4>
<p>A geographic heatmap helps to understand the distribution and density of=
 the given parameter on a map. The obvious application of geo heatmaps is w=
eather forecasting, but there are many more spheres where it can be used: r=
eal estate, commerce, transportation, healthcare, environmental science, an=
d many more.</p>
<h4><strong><em><span>When you shouldn't use a geographic heatmap</span></e=
m></strong></h4>
<p><span style=3D"font-size: 18px;">Geographical heatmaps have the same cor=
e drawbacks as regular heatmaps. It gives an approximate view and can lack =
important details. Extremes can dominate, which can sometimes be misleading=
. You should also take into consideration that geo heatmaps heavily rely on=
 colors. This means you should be really attentive to color palettes and ta=
ke <a href=3D"https://www.datylon.com/blog/data-visualization-for-colorblin=
d-readers">color blind viewers</a> into consideration while designing it.</=
span><br><br><a href=3D"https://www.datylon.com/blog/types-of-charts-graphs=
-examples-data-visualization#table-of-contents" rel=3D"noopener"><span styl=
e=3D"font-size: 14px;">Back to table of contents =E2=AC=86=EF=B8=8F</span><=
/a></p>
<a id=3D"choropleth-map" data-hs-anchor=3D"true"></a><hr>
<h3><br>Choropleth map</h3>
<h4><strong><em><span><br><img src=3D"https://www.datylon.com/hs-fs/hubfs/D=
atylon%20Website2020/Blogs/80%20types%20of%20charts%20and%20graphs/charts%2=
0iso%20links/80%20types%20of%20charts%20examples%20%E2%80%93%20Choropleth%2=
0map.png?width=3D600&amp;height=3D600&amp;name=3D80%20types%20of%20charts%2=
0examples%20%E2%80%93%20Choropleth%20map.png" width=3D"600" height=3D"600" =
loading=3D"lazy" alt=3D"80 types of charts examples =E2=80=93 Choropleth ma=
p" style=3D"height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 600px; margin-left: auto;=
 margin-right: auto; display: block;"><br><br>What is a choropleth map?</sp=
an></em></strong></h4>
<p>A choropleth map is a type of map in which different administrative area=
s are colored (or shaded) according to the magnitude of their numeric value=
. The main difference between a choropleth map and a geographic heatmap is =
that a choropleth map uses border-defined areas, such as countries, states,=
 or neighborhoods.&nbsp;</p>
<h4><strong><em><span>When should you use a choropleth map?</span></em></st=
rong></h4>
<p>Choropleth maps display geographical data using normalized values, makin=
g them ideal for illustrating various rates and ratios across different reg=
ions.</p>
<h4><strong><em><span>When you shouldn't use a choropleth map</span></em></=
strong></h4>
<p>Choropleth maps can be misleading when used to display raw data that is =
in some way connected to population. If a region has a high population, it =
might automatically show high absolute values for population-related indica=
tors. That=E2=80=99s why it=E2=80=99s important to use per-capita values fo=
r choropleth maps.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Sometimes, the size of the geographical area can be misleading, either i=
ncreasing or decreasing the perceived importance of the region. To minimize=
 this influence, you could consider alternatives such as tile maps, where a=
ll regions are represented by icons of the same size.<br><br><a href=3D"htt=
ps://www.datylon.com/blog/types-of-charts-graphs-examples-data-visualizatio=
n#table-of-contents" rel=3D"noopener"><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">Back=
 to table of contents =E2=AC=86=EF=B8=8F</span></a></p>
<a id=3D"tile-map" data-hs-anchor=3D"true"></a><hr>
<h3><br>Tile map</h3>
<p><img src=3D"https://www.datylon.com/hs-fs/hubfs/Datylon%20Website2020/Bl=
ogs/80%20types%20of%20charts%20and%20graphs/webp%20chart%20images/datylon-8=
0-types-of-charts-tile-map.webp?width=3D600&amp;height=3D600&amp;name=3Ddat=
ylon-80-types-of-charts-tile-map.webp" width=3D"600" height=3D"600" loading=
=3D"lazy" alt=3D"datylon-80-types-of-charts-tile-map" style=3D"height: auto=
; max-width: 100%; width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; dis=
play: block;"></p>
<p></p><div class=3D"hs-cta-embed hs-cta-simple-placeholder hs-cta-embed-18=
3856447613 hs-cta-embed__loaded" style=3D"max-width: 100%; max-height: 100%=
; width: 316px; height: 48.6111px; margin: 20px auto; display: block;" data=
-hubspot-wrapper-cta-id=3D"183856447613" align=3D"center">=20
 =20
<iframe src=3D"cid:frame-8D2F3A0CC3D24FF8EFC2C92F1AB01386@mhtml.blink" aria=
-label=3D"Embedded CTA" title=3D"Embedded CTA" allow=3D"autoplay; fullscree=
